<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:45:00 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>France gripped by latest summer heatwave as drought conditions worsen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260812-france-gripped-by-latest-summer-heatwave-as-drought-conditions-worsen</link><description>
Scorching heat continued to spread across most of mainland France on Wednesday, as the Ministry for Ecological Transition met to take stock of the effects of a drought that has been steadily worsening since May. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee532400-9624-11f1-9288-8fc7ca80b067</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:38:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4cd2ac0a-9033-11f1-8fa4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/FRANCE-RIVIERE-LOIRE-SECHERESSE.jpg">REUTERS - Stephane Mahe</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Total solar eclipse over Spain to draw millions of viewers across Europe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-total-solar-eclipse-over-spain-to-draw-millions-of-viewers-across-europe</link><description>
Large parts of north and central Spain, plus smaller parts of Portugal, Greenland and Iceland, will see a total solar eclipse on Wednesday – with the phenomenon also visible in the south of France. Starting near the North Pole before tracking south, the total eclipse will last up to two minutes and 18 seconds, with the partial eclipse visible across much of Western Europe, including the United Kingdom, Belgium, Switzerland and northern Italy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e825f6ee-956a-11f1-8575-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP670971115671.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e825f6ee-956a-11f1-8575-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP670971115671.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">acc22c2e-955d-11f1-9c3a-79acf86bd741</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:44:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e825f6ee-956a-11f1-8575-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP670971115671.jpg">AP - Andres Gutierrez</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Hungary elects Orban critic Andras Baka as first president in new political era</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260812-hungary-elects-orban-critic-andras-baka-as-first-president-of-new-political-era</link><description>
Hungarian lawmakers on Tuesday approved former supreme court chief Andras Baka – a prominent critic of Viktor Orban who was ousted during the ex-premier's time in power – as the country's next head of state.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">762bbf5c-9613-11f1-a50c-03e5429215e8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:36:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/44e5b510-9613-11f1-b9fe-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223528576693.jpg">Szilard Koszticsak/MTI via AP - Szilard Koszticsak</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Race to find Ebola vaccine as DR Congo outbreak kills more than 2,000</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260812-race-to-find-ebola-vaccine-as-dr-congo-outbreak-kills-more-than-2-000</link><description>
The latest outbreak of Ebola has killed more than 2,000 people in the Democratic Republic of Congo, according to health authorities. Meanwhile, international efforts have been stepped up to test a vaccine for the highly contagious haemorrhagic fever.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7534c1c2-962f-11f1-b43d-f3a546cf71d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:44:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/50759716-959a-11f1-af1b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26223437161951.jpg">AP Photo/Dieudonne Dirole - Dieudonne Dirole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Assisted dying, social media and agriculture put France’s top court in spotlight</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260811-assisted-dying-social-media-and-agriculture-put-france-s-top-court-in-spotlight</link><description>
France’s Constitutional Council is facing a politically charged end to the summer, with judges due to rule on a series of high-profile laws – including those covering assisted dying, social media use by children, agriculture and public security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">794857bc-956f-11f1-8018-6bca3bd6865c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:01:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c2265d6-9580-11f1-85dc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/conseil-constitutionnel-scaled.jpeg">© Christophe BONNET</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Lebanon becomes first country in Middle East to abolish death penalty</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-lebanon-becomes-first-country-in-middle-east-to-abolish-death-penalty</link><description>
Lebanon’s parliament on Tuesday abolished the death penalty, making it the first country in the Middle East to replace capital punishment with a sentence of life imprisonment with hard labour. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/600b5c90-1173-11ea-a781-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-01-12T103415Z_1319466856_GM1EB1C1FGL01_RTRMADP_3_LEBANON-PRISON.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/600b5c90-1173-11ea-a781-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-01-12T103415Z_1319466856_GM1EB1C1FGL01_RTRMADP_3_LEBANON-PRISON.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b65aa9ac-957e-11f1-844e-7385b0464f2f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:14:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/600b5c90-1173-11ea-a781-005056bf7c53/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-01-12T103415Z_1319466856_GM1EB1C1FGL01_RTRMADP_3_LEBANON-PRISON.JPG">REUTERS/Mohamed Azakir</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Former Syrian leader Assad sentenced to death in absentia over war crimes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-former-syrian-leader-assad-sentenced-to-death-in-absentia-over-war-crimes</link><description>
A Syrian court on Tuesday sentenced former ruler Bashar al-Assad to death after a trial in absentia, convicting him of atrocities committed during the country's civil war. Six of his closest aides were also handed death sentences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73c8abca-956f-11f1-aff4-e70fbbb452ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:58:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg">AFP - LOUAI BESHARA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and EU join international aid effort after Colombia earthquake</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-france-eu-join-international-aid-effort-after-colombia-earthquake</link><description>
France has joined the European Union and a host of countries in offering assistance to Colombia, where volunteers and rescuers are searching for survivors following Monday's deadly earthquake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e96a684-955e-11f1-bebd-75c492606bc4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:08:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg">© Jamie Saldarriaga / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>May ’68 protest leader Cohn-Bendit pledges support to Glucksmann for 2027</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260810-may-68-veteran-cohn-bendit-throws-support-behind-left-wing-glucksmann-for-2027</link><description>
Former Green MEP Daniel Cohn-Bendit, a historic figure on the French left, on Monday gave his support to Raphaël Glucksmann for France’s 2027 presidential election, in an interview with Le Point magazine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a90b0ffe-94b5-11f1-ba5c-c57808d5257e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:00:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg">AFP - LOU BENOIST</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rebel forces in Ethiopia's Tigray state condemn army drone strikes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260811-rebel-forces-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-state-condemn-army-drone-strikes</link><description>
Rebel authorities on Tuesday accused the Ethiopian government of carrying out deadly drone strikes in southern Tigray state and condemned the move as "a serious escalation", amid fears of a new war. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b05c8bea-9567-11f1-8107-913aa69e7026</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 13:25:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg">AFP - ABEL GEREZGIHER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Moscow and Damascus reach deal over Russian military bases in Syria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-moscow-and-damascus-reach-deal-over-russian-military-bases-in-syria</link><description>
Syria said on Sunday it had reached a deal with Moscow on the fate of Russia's two bases in the country, which it once used to provide military support to ousted leader Bashar al-Assad during the Syrian civil war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67a3afc4-9476-11f1-b20d-ffc054c909af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 04:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG">REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France introduces tough fines for unsolicited telemarketing calls</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260811-france-introduces-tough-fines-for-unsolicited-telemarketing-calls</link><description>
