</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0696e0c0-93f4-11f1-b693-771bd1b13781</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 05:56:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg">© Michael Sohn / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran says ‘Muslim Nato’ pact reflects retreat from US security umbrella</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-iran-says-muslim-nato-pact-reflects-retreat-from-us-security-umbrella</link><description>
Tehran has played down concerns over a new mutual defence pact between Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan, while portraying the agreement as evidence of declining regional reliance on the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">505d03ae-94b9-11f1-840e-457ddd2c08ca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:21:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Record temperatures swept regions home to 900 million people in July</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-record-temperatures-swept-regions-home-to-900-million-people-in-july</link><description>
Regions home to around 900 million people experienced their hottest July on record in 2026, including areas in the Sahel, Central America, France and Spain, according to analysis of Copernicus data.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13fd717a-949e-11f1-84b4-d34b2a11c752</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:33:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg">© Ina FASSBENDER / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghana backs Jamaica's petition to push UK for slavery reparations</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260810-monday-o-n-ghana-backs-jamaica-s-petition-to-push-uk-for-slavery-reparations</link><description>
Jamaica and Ghana, both former British colonies subjected to the transatlantic slave trade, are presenting a united front in the drive for reparatory justice. As Kingston prepares to lodge a formal petition with King Charles III seeking to advance its claim for reparations from the United Kingdom, Ghana's president says the global movement to address the legacy of slavery has reached a "defining moment". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66eb257c-91aa-11f1-aa99-717baab8f235</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:01:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg">AFP - RICARDO MAKYN</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Outsiders Malawi beat Ghana to reach WAFCON semi-finals and World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260810-outsiders-malawi-beat-ghana-to-reach-wafcon-semi-finals-and-world-cup</link><description>
Malawi have completed one of the biggest surprises in Women’s Africa Cup of Nations history, coming from behind to beat Ghana 2-1 and secure both a place in the semi-finals and qualification for the 2027 Women’s World Cup.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6eb2671a-94e4-11f1-b780-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Malawi-Wafon.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6eb2671a-94e4-11f1-b780-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Malawi-Wafon.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">741c5b86-94e2-11f1-b541-a5d0b1ee70af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:54:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6eb2671a-94e4-11f1-b780-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Malawi-Wafon.jpg">© WAFCON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>EU athletics to apply new TV guidelines on non-sexualisation of women</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260810-eu-athletics-comp-to-apply-new-tv-guidelines-on-non-sexualisation-of-women</link><description>
New guidelines to prevent broadcasters sexualising coverage of women athletes will come into place when the European championships start in Birmingham on Monday. 
